# Settings of this site: copy to site.env and edit. Start.ps1 does the copy for you on the first
# run and then stops so that you can fill it in. site.env holds addresses and contact details but
# no secrets; it is read by the app, the worker and the egress proxy, and git ignores it.

# The public address of Kal (the Cloudflare tunnel's public hostname). Invite and reset links
# printed by Cal.ps1 start with it.
BASE_URL=https://cal.example.org

# Contact details sent to Open Food Facts (in the User-Agent) and to the push services.
OFF_CONTACT=admin@example.org
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:admin@example.org

# Your Mealie and openGym servers. Leave a line out (or empty) to turn that integration off.
# Only people on this server's Kal can use them, and only the address set here is ever called.
# The addresses must be https; the egress proxy lets Kal reach exactly these two hosts.
# MEALIE_BASE_URL=https://mealie.example.org
# OPENGYM_BASE_URL=https://gym.example.org

# Optional: more hosts the egress proxy should allow, comma separated, plain host names without
# https:// (a leading dot also allows subdomains). Restart the egress container after a change.
# PUSH_SERVICE_HOSTS=
# EGRESS_EXTRA_HOSTS=

# The Kal Android app (README "Kal for Android"): its package name (the kal.appId it was built
# with) and the SHA-256 fingerprint of its signing certificate as scripts/android-build.mjs prints
# it (several comma separated). Together they make /.well-known/assetlinks.json, which lets the app
# open Kal full screen. Put kal.apk and version.json in the android folder next to this file.
# ANDROID_APP_ID=app.kal
# ANDROID_CERT_SHA256=
